==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|a}}

===Etymology===
An old Baltic loan; derived from the same word from which e.g. Lithuanian {{term|gaũras|lang=lt}} is descended. Cognates include Veps and Estonian {{term|lang=et|karv}} and Livonian {{term|lang=liv|kōra}}. Originally ''karva'' only had the meaning "color". In its current meaning it is first mentioned in a biblical text in 1621.<ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2004}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈkɑrʋɑ]|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|kar|va|lang=fi}}
